/* Russian menu/UI text, keyed by the exact compiled US literal that reaches
 * Gfx_StringDraw. Included by lang_ru.c; see lang_ru.h for why the port has to
 * carry its own translation rather than read the disc's.
 *
 * Writing rules:
 * - '_' is the rendered space. A literal ' ' (0x20) falls through the drawer
 *   untouched and advances nothing, so it must never appear inside a value.
 * - No Latin letters. Every one of these patches repaints the Latin cells with
 *   Cyrillic, so "FPS" would draw as "ЕПС". Digits and punctuation keep their
 *   own cells and are safe.
 * - Keys keep their '\x07' colour prefix and '\x01' kerning bytes exactly as
 *   the compiled literal has them; values keep the '\x07' and drop the '\x01'.
 * - Several draw sites pass a fixed glyph budget rather than the string length,
 *   and the drawer stops once that many glyphs are drawn. Budgets noted per
 *   block below — values must not exceed them or they render truncated. */

